The search wasn't very helpful. Let me look at the actual upstream fix for this fribidi bug. Let me check the git blame or look at the fribidi GitHub for the fix commit. Let me look at the code around the PDI handling once more and think about the exact trigger.

Let me reconsider. The key issue is that `isolate_level--` happens in the PDI branch when `valid_isolate_count > 0`. The fix would be to guard it with `if (isolate_level > 0)`.

Let me reconsider how to get `valid_isolate_count > 0` while `isolate_level == 0`. 

Actually, let me reconsider the FSI handling more carefully. In FSI, the search loop:
```c
for_run_list (fsi_pp, pp)
{
  if (RL_TYPE(fsi_pp) == FRIBIDI_TYPE_PDI)
  {
    isolate_count--;
    if (valid_isolate_count < 0)
      break;
  }
  else if (FRIBIDI_IS_ISOLATE(RL_TYPE(fsi_pp)))
    isolate_count++;
  else if (isolate_count==0 && FRIBIDI_IS_LETTER (RL_TYPE (fsi_pp)))
  {
    fsi_base_level = FRIBIDI_DIR_TO_LEVEL (RL_TYPE (fsi_pp));
    break;
  }
}
```

This is a search for a local strong character. It uses local `isolate_count`. Not directly relevant.

